{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"c1127791-5c79-483d-97bf-f67a828c3293","title":"Unit circle and the sine wave"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c1127791-5c79-483d-97bf-f67a828c3293","step":{"id":"s1","script":"On the unit circle, an angle starts at the positive horizontal axis. The point’s vertical coordinate is the sine of that angle.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"circle","region":"left","frame":{"x":[-1.4,1.4],"y":[-1.4,1.4],"axes":"origin","equal_scale":true,"x_label":"x","y_label":"y"},"marks":[{"kind":"circle","id":"unit","center":[0,0],"r":1},{"kind":"point","id":"origin","at":[0,0]},{"kind":"point","id":"moving","at":[0.8660254,0.5],"label":"P"},{"kind":"segment","id":"radius","from":{"at":"origin"},"to":{"at":"moving"}},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"moving"},"to":[0.8660254,0],"stroke":"dashed","label":"sin θ"},{"kind":"arc","center":[0,0],"r":0.3,"start":0,"end":30,"label":"θ"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"coordinates","anchor":{"el":"circle","side":"below","gap":0.03},"latex":"P=(\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta)"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c1127791-5c79-483d-97bf-f67a828c3293","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Now put angle on the horizontal axis and height on the vertical axis. Tracking that height draws the sine wave.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"wave","region":"right","frame":{"x":[0,6.283185307],"y":[-1.35,1.35],"axes":"edge","x_label":"θ (radians)","y_label":"sin θ"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"sine","y":"sin(x)","domain":[0,6.283185307]},{"kind":"point","id":"sample","at":{"on":"sine","x":0.523598776}},{"kind":"segment","from":[0.523598776,0],"to":{"at":"sample"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[1.05,0.25],"text":"(π/6, 1/2)","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"samplevalue","anchor":{"el":"coordinates","side":"below","gap":0.03},"latex":"\\sin(\\pi/6)=\\tfrac12"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"c1127791-5c79-483d-97bf-f67a828c3293","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s3"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c1127791-5c79-483d-97bf-f67a828c3293","step":{"id":"s3","script":"After a quarter turn, the circle point reaches its highest position. The sine wave therefore reaches one at pi over two.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"topcircle","on":"circle","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"top","at":[0,1],"label":"π/2"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"origin"},"to":{"at":"top"},"stroke":"dashed"}]},{"op":"figure","id":"peakwave","on":"wave","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"peak","at":{"on":"sine","x":1.570796327},"label":"(π/2, 1)"},{"kind":"segment","from":[1.570796327,0],"to":{"at":"peak"},"stroke":"dashed"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c1127791-5c79-483d-97bf-f67a828c3293","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Continue around: zero, negative one, then zero again. One full turn gives one complete wave, which repeats every two pi radians.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"finishcircle","on":"circle","marks":[{"kind":"point","at":[-1,0],"label":"π"},{"kind":"point","at":[0,-1],"label":"3π/2"},{"kind":"point","at":[1,0],"label":"0, 2π"}]},{"op":"figure","id":"finishwave","on":"wave","marks":[{"kind":"point","at":{"on":"sine","x":0}},{"kind":"point","at":{"on":"sine","x":3.141592654},"label":"π"},{"kind":"point","id":"trough","at":{"on":"sine","x":4.71238898},"label":"(3π/2, −1)"},{"kind":"segment","from":[4.71238898,0],"to":{"at":"trough"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"point","at":{"on":"sine","x":6.283185307},"label":"2π"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"period","anchor":{"el":"samplevalue","side":"below","gap":0.03},"latex":"\\sin(\\theta+2\\pi)=\\sin\\theta"}],"checkpoint":null}}
